  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A sample of liquid X with mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2m\"></span> and temperature <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60^\\circ\\text{C}\"></span> is mixed with a sample of liquid Y with mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> and temperature <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10^\\circ\\text{C}\"></span> in a perfectly insulated container. The final equilibrium temperature of the mixture is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30^\\circ\\text{C}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\text{specific heat capacity of liquid X}}{\\text{specific heat capacity of liquid Y}}\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{3}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3\"></span></p></li></ol>"
